# /etc/sudoers.d/station-netwatch -- the station Wi-Fi watchdog's root
# actions (issue #686), and nothing else. Install with a syntax check, never
# a plain cp (a broken sudoers file locks sudo out):
#
#     sudo visudo -cf ~/aviary/Servers/station-netwatch.sudoers
#     sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g root ~/aviary/Servers/station-netwatch.sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/station-netwatch
#
# Why sudo lines and not a root unit: todd's sudo asks for a password, and
# flyway/netwatch.py lives in the todd-owned checkout that station-autodeploy
# updates from GitHub. A root unit would run that tree as root every two
# minutes -- a new todd-to-root path. These lines grant only: bounce a wl*
# network device, unbind/bind a USB device, reboot. No file writes outside
# those two sysfs files, no shell, no editor. (sudo's * also matches spaces,
# so the nmcli lines could name extra devices -- a disconnect, never more.)
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/nmcli device disconnect wl*, \
                          /usr/bin/nmcli device connect wl*, \
                          /usr/bin/tee /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usb/unbind, \
                          /usr/bin/tee /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usb/bind, \
                          /usr/bin/systemctl reboot
